proof.text:
For witnesses fix the finite ring $P_n$. The comparison inverse image $
u_T^*$ is exact and commutes with cohomology. More explicitly exactness preserves the kernels and cokernels in the good truncation formulas, so termwise $
u_T^*	au^{\le m}=	au^{\le m}
u_T^*$ and $
u_T^*	au^{\ge m+1}=	au^{\ge m+1}
u_T^*$, naturally; these identifications descend through quasi-isomorphisms. Applying them to $\alpha_n$ gives the claimed levelwise origins and compatibility with all strict transitions. The truncated etale objects are still bounded below: truncating a bounded-below cohomological interval retains its lower bound or replaces it by $m+1$. This proves the unconditional, levelwise part of the witness clause.
